{"conversation_id":"0a755610-0c73-4d9d-ac97-2d730e307b2a","status":"SUCCESS","response":"# TDD RED — Regression Tests for 3 Live-Verified Defects\n\n### Summary of Changes\nWritten and committed the regression test suite covering the 3 live-verified defects in [`tests/regression-defects.test.ts`](file:///home/bhd/Documents/Projects/bhd/cmd-pallet/tests/regression-defects.test.ts). No production code was modified.\n\n---\n\n### Regression Test Coverage\n\n1. **D1: Qualified-Name Resolvability**\n   - Direct resolution of candidate names (`read claude:dup-command`, `read codex:dup-command`, `read /claude:dup-command`) to render content with exit code 0.\n   - Execution of qualified candidate names (`run claude:dup-command \u003cargs\u003e`, `run codex:dup-command \u003cargs\u003e`) to render `Invoked: /...` and interpolated body.\n   - Ambiguity round-trip contract: all candidates returned in ambiguity list (`json.candidates`) are verified to be directly resolvable via `read` and `run`.\n   - JSON flag support for qualified names (`read claude:dup-command --json`, `run claude:dup-command --json`).\n\n2. **D2: Binary-Level Exit-Code Contracts \u0026 Execution**\n   - Non-existent / missing command name for `read` \u0026 `run` spawns binary and verifies exit code `1` with `\"not found\"` on stderr/stdout.\n   - Ambiguous commands for `read` \u0026 `run` spawn binary and verify exit code `1` with candidates listed on stderr.\n   - Missing arguments for `read` \u0026 `run` spawn binary and verify usage error exit code `2`.\n   - Search / list queries with no matches spawn binary and verify exit code `1`.\n   - Valid command `read` \u0026 `run` spawn binary and verify exit code `0`.\n\n3. **D3: Duplicate Output Deduplication (`search` \u0026 `list`)**\n   - `list` text output contains no duplicate lines for the same command name.\n   - `search \u003cquery\u003e` text output contains no duplicate lines when multiple scopes define the command.\n   - `list --json` and `search \u003cquery\u003e --json` return deduplicated arrays with unique command names.\n   - Synthetic 3-scope fixture (`claude`, `codex`, `gemini` sharing identical `deploy-sync` command) verifies `search` output emits the command exactly once.\n\n---\n\n### Vitest Test Results\n\n```\nTest Files  1 failed | 9 passed (10)\n     Tests  19 failed | 84 passed (103)\n```\n- **Existing Tests**: 84 passed (100% green across all 9 pre-existing test files).\n- **New Regression Tests**: 19 failed (100% RED across D1, D2, and D3).\n\n---\n\n### Git Commit\n- **Commit**: `09395ec` — `RED: regression tests for qualified-name, exit-codes, dupes` (unpushed).\n","duration_seconds":655.815095752,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":230736,"output_tokens":30123,"thinking_tokens":15742,"cache_read_tokens":2212815,"total_tokens":260859}}
